From Alexis.Gabadinho at unige.ch  Wed May  5 11:20:37 2010
From: Alexis.Gabadinho at unige.ch (Alexis Gabadinho)
Date: Wed, 05 May 2010 11:20:37 +0200
Subject: [Traminer-users] seqdplot et pourcentages
Message-ID: <4BE13865.1010106@unige.ch>

Hi Claire,

You can use therefore the "with.missing=TRUE" argument. With this option 
the transversal distributions  include the missing state, and this state 
appears on the plot with a dedicated color.

Here is an example:

data(ex1)
ex1.seq <- seqdef(ex1, 1:13)
seqdplot(ex1.seq, with.missing=TRUE)

All the best,
Alexis.


